Predecessor and third-party material
------------------------------------

This integration succeeds the custom component MrMooreUK/fluvalble
(https://github.com/MrMooreUK/fluvalble, Apache License 2.0, Copyright MrMooreUK
and contributors). It keeps its domain (fluvalble), its configuration entry
format and its unique IDs, so existing installations can switch over. The two
integrations cannot be installed at the same time.

The connection, command and state handling were written anew. The following
parts are derived from MrMooreUK/fluvalble under the Apache License 2.0:

- custom_components/fluvalble/products.py: the product table (product IDs,
  model names, channel order) and the CIE XYZ spectrum tables, from
  core/products.py and core/color.py.
- custom_components/fluvalble/color.py: the colour fit (non-negative mix of at
  most three channels in CIE XYZ), adapted from core/color.py.
- The decoding of the product ID from the Bluetooth advertisement, from
  core/products.py.

MrMooreUK/fluvalble credits the Plant PRO Bluetooth protocol research and
hardware validation to cryystyy
(https://github.com/cryystyy/fluval-plant-pro-4-homeassistant, MIT License).
No code from that project is included here; the Plant PRO entry in the product
table comes from the MrMooreUK/fluvalble table.

Protocol source
---------------

The Bluetooth protocol (FFF0 service, D1/D2 CBOR frames, clock packet, CBOR
keys), the product IDs and the LED spectrum data come from the official
FluvalConnect app (eu.hagen.fluvalconnect), studied for interoperability.
No code or assets of the app are included.

The Fluval logo in custom_components/fluvalble/brand/, assets/ and docs/ is
the official logo of Fluval, used only to identify the supported devices.

